# Confidentiality denylist for the leak-guard — FORMAT EXAMPLE ONLY.
#
# One case-insensitive regex per line; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Copy this to `.leakpatterns` (which is git-ignored) and replace the placeholders below with
# your real customer / domain terms. The real `.leakpatterns` is NEVER committed — that is the
# whole point: the operative denylist must live outside the committed artifact so this repo
# cannot be reversed to reveal the domain it protects.
#
# In CI, materialise `.leakpatterns` from a repository secret before running the guard
# (see .github/workflows/compliance-gate.yml).
#
# Example placeholders (replace these):
# \bacmecorp\b
# \bwidget[- ]?works\b
# \bproject[- ]?falcon\b
